   "id": "spcpt_5KxxFcs2n8fKDzMb",
   "name": "Reciprocal Graphs - Sketching",
   "definition": null,
   "video_id": "815590308"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Sketching reciprocal curves"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "What are reciprocal graphs?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Reciprocal graphs involve equations with an $x$ term on the denominator e.g. $\\frac{1}{x}$\n- There are two basic reciprocal graphs to know for A level"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "** **$y=\\frac{1}{x}$** **and  $y=\\frac{1}{x^{2}}$** **"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- The second one of these is always positive ![Reciprocal Graphs - Sketching Notes Diagram 1, A Level & AS Level Pure Maths Revision Notes](assets/e7d70389b289-2-7-2-reciprocal-graphs-sketching-notes-diagram-.png)"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "More reciprocal graphs"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- You also need to recognise graphs where the numerator is not one"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/06/2.7.2-Reciprocal-Graphs-Sketching-Notes-Diagram-2.png",
   "file": "assets/1919582c9893-2-7-2-reciprocal-graphs-sketching-notes-diagram-.png",
   "alt": "Reciprocal Graphs - Sketching Notes Diagram 2, A Level & AS Level Pure Maths Revision Notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- The **sign** of **a** shows which part of the graph the curves are located"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "The **size** of **a** shows how steep the curves are"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- The closer **a** is to 0 the more **L-shaped** the curves are"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/06/2.7.2-Reciprocal-Graphs-Sketching-Notes-Diagram-3.png",
   "file": "assets/63a67d52b307-2-7-2-reciprocal-graphs-sketching-notes-diagram-.png",
   "alt": "Reciprocal Graphs - Sketching Notes Diagram 3, A Level & AS Level Pure Maths Revision Notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- All have two *asymptotes*\n\n  - horizontal, **y = 0** (**x**-axis)\n  - vertical, **x = 0** (**y**-axis)"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I sketch a reciprocal graph?"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/06/2.7.2-Reciprocal-Graphs-Sketching-Notes-Diagram-4.png",
   "file": "assets/c6386995656d-2-7-2-reciprocal-graphs-sketching-notes-diagram-.png",
   "alt": "Reciprocal Graphs - Sketching Notes Diagram 4, A Level & AS Level Pure Maths Revision Notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- **STEP 1**\nUse the sign of “a” to locate the curves and use the size of “a” to gauge the steepness of the curve\n- **STEP 2**\nSketch the graph\n- **STEP 3**\nLabel the points **x = 1** and **x = -1** as a guide to the scale of your graph\n- **STEP 4**\nDraw **asymptotes** with **dotted** lines\n- These graphs do not intercept either axis\n- **Graph** **transformations** of them could cross the axes (see Translations)"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "worked-example",
   "label": "Worked Example",
